<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech central bank leaves rates unchanged.</title>
<headline>Czech central bank leaves rates unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech central bank board left interest rates unchanged after its regular weekly meeting on Thursday.</p>
<p>The board said in a statement that favourable movement in the country's inflation rate and money supply had allowed it too ease minimum reserve requirements to 9.5 percent from 11.5 percent, effective May 8.</p>
<p>It made no comment on any changes to rates despite widespread market speculation that a rate cut was on the cards.</p>
</text>
